; The parcels the buildable region is derived over, none of which says anywhere
; what is buildable on it: a plot is four corners, four edges, a loop and a setback
; claimed on each edge, and what may be built is read back out of those every time
; the question is asked.

; A rectangular plot with a different setback on every side of it: six metres at
; the road, four at the rear and three at each flank. Nothing here says which is
; which — each number is written on the edge it governs.
(vertex geom:V-101
  (label "Corner plot, south-west corner")
  (frame frame:site)
  (position
    (value (0.0 0.0 0.0) m)
    (source "Boundary survey BS-2026-01, Acme Surveys")
    (method method:total-station)
    (accuracy (independent 0.004 m) (systematic 0.008 m control:CP-1))
    (date "2026-03-11")))
(vertex geom:V-102
  (label "Corner plot, south-east corner")
  (frame frame:site)
